Z||000002||Seanh||10-01-2001||11:24 PM||||You use the 3.4 Block and bottem end. You use the Fiero oil pan and timing chain cover, heads, intake, and all accessories. The starter needs to be drilled on the other side of the block, other then that its drop in and go..<P>Oh yeah, you need a flywheel/flexplate from an 88 Fiero...<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto, getting ready to install T-6 turbo.||||reg||1
